From ddaaf200d06bf79cf3f18a477c3543f590326e73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 07:55:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 75/75] perf(ultra_honk): let Chonk's prover instances free the
 circuit data they have copied

ProverInstance_ takes CopiedCircuitData; with RELEASE (Chonk in release builds) the lookup polynomials
are built before the trace and the lookup tables with their gate records are freed right after, and
populate fills the selectors first so that the parallel wire pass frees each trace block once its last row
chunk has been copied; the copy-cycle phases after it read only the recorded cells and the blocks' sizes
and offsets. The default (KEEP) leaves the circuit intact for checks and VK recomputation.
